I found and resolved the bug causing the ASCII art to not display!

### Root Cause
Initially, the player starts in the Town Hub (`floor: 0`). When you click the **"Look around..."** action from the start screen, the code evaluated `wasInSameArea` as `true` (since you were technically already on floor 0). 
This passed `preservePosition = true` to `startDungeon()`, which bypassed the `loadMap(0)` call. Because `loadMap` was skipped on the initial startup, the map array (`currentMap`) remained uninitialized (`[]`), leaving the map viewport completely empty.

### The Fix
I updated the [startDungeon](file:///C:/Users/jenar/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/tower_manager/game.js#L200) function to explicitly check if the map has not yet been loaded (`currentMap.length === 0`). If it is empty, it will force-initialize the map data, even if position preservation is enabled:
```javascript
function startDungeon(preservePosition = false) {
    switchMode('dungeon');
    if (!preservePosition || currentMap.length === 0) {
        loadMap(player.floor);
    }
    dungeonLogEl.innerText = player.floor === 0 ? "You explore the Town Square..." : "You explore the dangerous Tower...";
    renderMap();
}
```

Please refresh your browser window and click **"Look around..."** on the main menu, and you will see the fully rendered, color-coded ASCII Town Square!

